      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Row 100, glossy abelia. GBIF treats Abelia x grandiflora as a synonym of Abelia chinensis, and NC State's page cached for it is the Chinese abelia (A. chinensis, the parent species), so it stands in for the hybrid; RHS has a page for the hybrid itself. Two care sources only, no Missouri BG page (the search found none) and no ASPCA page. Agree on full sun (NC State also part shade), moist well-drained soil and a semi-evergreen to deciduous shrub that may die back in the cold. Size: RHS 2.5 to 4 m, 'shrub to 3 m' in its own description; NC State 5 to 8 ft by 4 to 6 ft; 300 by 300 cm follows the RHS description. Hardiness H5 is the RHS rating (it also says not fully hardy, sheltered position). Dormancy 'winter' because semi-evergreen/deciduous in cold. Toxicity: neither page states any, so people and pets stay unknown. Es and it names are machine drafts."
      },
